invariant: INV-51
file: Makefile
catches: test/lint-schedule-order.sh
reason: the Makefile no longer gives sha512_avx2.c -fno-schedule-insns2
  where gcc compiles for x86-64, which is how the build reads to anybody
  who knows that the flag changes no digest. gcc 13.3's second scheduling
  pass then moves each schedule step's vector instructions in among those
  of one or two rounds and leaves up to 99 instructions on general
  registers in a row with none, and SHA-384 over 16 KiB takes 1 to 4
  percent longer by the CPU model. Every test of what the kernel computes
  passes. make lint-schedule-order asks make for the commands a gcc build
  for x86-64 runs, on every machine, and requires the flag in the two
  that compile sha512_avx2.c. Where $(CC) is gcc for x86-64 it also reads
  the assembly those two commands write and finds the long run.

--- old
SHA512_AVX2_GCC_CFLAGS := $(if $(GCC_X86_64_TARGET),-fno-schedule-insns2)
--- new
SHA512_AVX2_GCC_CFLAGS :=
